      "terminal": "\u25cf Before I write it, here is the shape I have in mind. I have sketched it into\n  the tree as three features so you can see where each piece would live and say\n  what you want kept.\n\n  \u00b7 Rule settings \u2014 every value the rules read, in one file you edit rather\n    than constants spread through the modules.\n  \u00b7 Statement periods \u2014 the month lined up on the date a payment was made,\n    the week on the date the bank posted it.\n  \u00b7 Weekly spending summary \u2014 the same summary at a finer grain, written\n    beside the monthly one rather than over it.",
      "propose": [
        {
          "kind": "add_node",
          "title": "Rule settings",
          "description": "Gathers every value the rules read \u2014 the merchant patterns, what happens to a merchant nothing matches, which date each summary is lined up on \u2014 into one file the reader edits instead of constants spread through the modules. Nothing supplies a default for a missing value: a file with a piece missing stops the run and says which piece.",
          "before": "f-007dec9d",
          "rationale": "plan: the categories cannot be managed without editing the source while each module owns its own constants"
        },
        {
          "kind": "add_node",
          "title": "Statement periods",
          "description": "Decides which period a transaction belongs to, for a month and for a week. The month is lined up on the date the payment was made and the week on the date the bank posted it, because the two are read for different reasons: a month answers what was spent in January, and a week is read next to the statement the bank sends.",
          "before": "f-007dec9d",
          "rationale": "plan: a finer grain than a month needs a period the summary can be grouped by"
        },
        {
          "kind": "add_node",
          "title": "Weekly spending summary",
          "description": "The same summary at a finer grain, grouped into weeks and written beside the monthly one rather than over it, so both are readable at once. Recurring payments stay counted in months whichever summary is being read, because that is about when a commitment falls.",
          "parent": "f-007dec9d",
          "rationale": "plan: the request is to see spending at a finer grain than a whole month"
        }
      ],
